---
import Entry from "../components/Entry.astro";
import { plate } from "./_shared/plates";

const markup = `<section data-scene data-scene-at="0.34 0.67" style="--len: 3">
  <div data-scene-stage>
    <div data-scene-beats>
      <div data-scene-beat>…</div>
      <div data-scene-beat>…</div>
      <div data-scene-beat>…</div>
    </div>
    <figure data-scene-aside>…</figure>  <!-- steps out of sight on a phone -->
    <span data-scene-progress></span>
  </div>
</section>`;
const beatsCopy = [
  { n: "01", title: "Il palco resta fermo.", text: "La sezione è alta tre schermi: mentre la scorri, il palco rimane sullo schermo." },
  { n: "02", title: "Il testo cambia, una battuta alla volta.", text: "Ogni battuta lascia il posto alla successiva in un punto preciso dello scroll." },
  { n: "03", title: "La riga in fondo dice quanto manca.", text: "Quando la sezione finisce, il palco riprende a scorrere con la pagina." },
];
---

<Entry
  id="stage"
  markup={markup}
  look="Scorri: il palco resta sullo schermo per tre schermi di scroll, le battute si passano la parola a un terzo e a due terzi, la riga in fondo si riempie. Tornando su, tutto torna indietro."
  replay={false}
  attributes={[
    { name: "--len", value: "3", what: "How many screens of scroll the scene lasts (default 2.5)." },
    { name: "data-scene-at", value: "0.34 0.67", what: "When each beat hands over to the next, as shares of the scene (evenly spaced without it)." },
    { name: "data-scene-aside", value: "—", what: "Secondary content that steps out of sight on a phone's stage (screen readers keep it)." },
  ]}
>
  <section class="sg" data-scene data-scene-at="0.34 0.67" style="--len: 3">
    <div class="sg-stage" data-scene-stage>
      <div class="wrap sg-grid">
        <div class="sg-beats" data-scene-beats>
          {
            beatsCopy.map((b) => (
              <div class="sg-beat" data-scene-beat>
                <p class="sg-n">{b.n} / 03</p>
                <h3 class="sg-title">{b.title}</h3>
                <p class="sg-text">{b.text}</p>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </div>
        <figure class="sg-plate" data-scene-aside>
          <img src={plate(61)} alt="Una tavola in stile cianografia." width="1200" height="900" />
        </figure>
      </div>
      <span class="sg-progress" data-scene-progress aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="wrap sg-after">
    <p>Dopo la sezione la pagina riprende normale: il palco è CSS (sticky), senza spazi aggiunti dallo script.</p>
  </div>
</Entry>

<style>
  .sg {
    --scene-gutter: var(--gutter);
    --scene-progress-color: var(--blue);
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--on-ink);
  }
  .sg-stage {
    padding-block: clamp(72px, 12vh, 120px);
  }
  .sg-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 6fr) minmax(0, 5fr);
    align-items: center;
    gap: clamp(32px, 5vw, 80px);
    width: 100%;
  }
  .sg-beats {
    display: grid;
    gap: 48px;
  }
  .sg-n {
    margin: 0 0 18px;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--blue);
  }
  .sg-title {
    margin: 0 0 18px;
    max-width: 13em;
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(32px, 4.4vw, 64px);
    line-height: 0.98;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
  }
  .sg-text {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 30em;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--on-ink-mute);
  }
  .sg-plate {
    margin: 0;
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 3;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid var(--on-ink-rule);
  }
  .sg-plate img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
  }
  .sg-after {
    padding-block: clamp(64px, 10vh, 120px) clamp(160px, 26vh, 280px);
  }
  .sg-after p {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 34em;
    color: var(--mute-2);
  }
  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .sg-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .sg-title {
      font-size: clamp(30px, 9vw, 40px);
    }
  }
</style>
